orithmic outputs as legally binding. Bypassing evaluation bureaucracy through hardware proxies simply shifts the locus of failure from the testing lab to the courtroom, where judges and juries are left to sort out liability without a documented trail of domain-specific validation. Effective governance requires strengthening the institutional oversight bodies that review deployed behavior, matching the rigor of financial auditing and medical device clearance rather than chasing hardware shadows.",
